    "reading": {
        "body": "Of twelve tracked AI API providers, eleven were healthy as of September 2, 2026, but the providers are not equally reliable over the roughly three-week observation window: Lambda's healthy rate was 42.1 percent against a field where every other provider cleared 86.7 percent.\n\nThat gap is the one signal this data actually supports. Ten of the twelve providers, AssemblyAI, Cerebras, Cohere, Deepgram, ElevenLabs, Groq, and Stability AI among them, report healthy rates at or above 94 percent, several at a perfect 100. OpenAI, at 86.7 percent, and Fireworks AI, at 94.7 percent, sit below that cluster but still far above Lambda. A provider whose infrastructure this site elsewhere counts on for inference capacity showing uptime below half its observation window is a compute reliability signal, not a model-quality one, and it says nothing about why Lambda's rate is low.\n\nThe daily healthy-provider count stayed at 11 or 12 for most of the window, dipping only to 10 on two dates in mid-to-late August, so the aggregate figure is stable even though the underlying per-provider rates are not. This is an uptime tally alone, with no data here on incident causes, response times, or remediation.",
